# Auto-commit

After finishing a coherent unit of work (feature, fix, or refactor), create a git commit immediately. Do not wait for the user to ask.

- Commit only project source changes; never commit `.env`, credentials, or secrets.
- Use concise commit messages in the repo's existing style (imperative, focused on why).
- Do not push to remote unless the user asks or the task explicitly requires it.
- If there is nothing to commit, skip silently.
